// SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
// examples/pico/repl_demo/repl_demo.u
//
// Interactive REPL workload for the v0.9.4 Pi Pico demo.  Baked into
// C via tools/urbi-compile-stdlib-pico; the resulting array is loaded
// by main.c at boot and exposed on the Lobby.
//
// Connect via USB CDC (/dev/ttyACM0) or UART0 (GP0/GP1 @ 115200 8N1).
// See README.md for sample sessions.
//
// BSP surface (FLAT — v0.7.1 embedding API limit, no sub-object
// installer; that's a v1.x property API gap):
//   led_on()      led_off()     led_toggle()    led_pwm(duty)
//   temp_celsius() => float
//   button_pressed() => bool
//   tick event    pressed event

// MINIMAL — v0.9.4 Pico bring-up.  Just install the button watcher.
//
// echo() is deferred: the v0.9.1 echo is a LobbyMethods method that
// requires a per-session Lobby, and this v0.9.4 Pico build skips the
// REPL service entirely (heap doesn't fit — see main.c + design-risks).
// Without echo, the watcher just toggles the LED; press BOOTSEL = LED
// flips.  That's the demo's user-visible interaction.
//
// Restore echo() and the at(temp_celsius()...) watchers once the v1.x
// lightweight-session REPL lands.
whenever (pressed) {
    led_toggle()
}

// NOTE 1: top-level echo() calls were removed during v0.9.4 bring-up
// because `echo` is a LobbyMethods method that requires a Lobby
// instance — Lobby is created per-REPL-session, not at boot.  echo()
// INSIDE watcher bodies works fine: it resolves at fire time when a
// session exists.  Filed v1.x: "boot-time banner / no-Lobby echo".
//
// NOTE 2: the bare-prefix tag labels (`greet:`, `temp_watch_hot:`,
// `temp_watch_cool:`) were stripped — the v0.9.4 parser/runtime treats
// the prefix as a GETSLOT on an existing slot, not as a new-tag
// declaration.  This is a v1.x deferral.  Without the
// prefix the watchers still install + fire, but cannot be `.stop()`'d
// individually.  Restore once tag-prefix labels + Tag.new() land.
//
// On connect, try: temp_celsius() / led_on() / led_off() to verify
// the verb surface.
